  "body_html": "<h1>Maximin and Minimax Values</h1>\n<p>For a mixed row strategy $x$, player I's guarantee is the worst expected payoff\nagainst a pure column:</p>\n<p>$$\\gamma_I(x) = \\min_{j \\in J} E_A(x,j).$$</p>\n<p>For a mixed column strategy $y$, player II's guarantee against player I is the\nlargest payoff player I can obtain from a pure row:</p>\n<p>$$\\gamma_{II}(y) = \\max_{i \\in I} E_A(i,y).$$</p>\n<p>The maximin value is \\(\\sup_x \\gamma_I(x)\\), and the minimax value is\n\\(\\inf_y \\gamma_{II}(y)\\).</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Chapter 2, Definitions 2.2.2-2.2.6] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>, <code>references/MechDesign.pdf</code>. Guarantees, maxmin, minmax, and game value.</li>\n</ul>",
